menu "Firmware updates"

    config PANEL_OTA_DEVICE
        string "Device name the update server knows this board by (empty: the board's id)"
        default ""
        help
            The "device" a check sends to the update server (docs/features/13 OTA-018): the
            server's catalogue names a board by its product, for example "crowpanel_dhe04107d"
            for the CrowPanel Advanced 7" (set in its sdkconfig.defaults). Empty uses the board's
            id from its description (board_info()->id, for example "crowpanel_p4"), which backups
            use too and which stays as it is.

    config PANEL_OTA_DEFAULT_DOMAIN
        string "Update server (a domain)"
        default "roboalarms.com"
        help
            This build's own update server (OTA-017): the panel asks https://firmware.<domain>.
            The installer can choose another one (its signing key is then checked and confirmed,
            OTA-020); a panel with no choice stored, or a damaged one, uses this. Empty: no
            automatic checks until a server is chosen.

    config PANEL_OTA_CHECK_HOURS
        int "Check for updates every (hours)"
        range 0 720
        default 24
        help
            Only checks and shows what is available; installing always needs a person
            (panel, Home Assistant or console). 0 = check only on request.

    config PANEL_OTA_CP_AUTO
        bool "Update the Wi-Fi co-processor from the cp_fw partition automatically"
        default y
        help
            When the image in "cp_fw" differs from what the co-processor runs, send it once
            the system is idle (OTA-007). A failed attempt is not repeated automatically.

endmenu
